<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Cadurci</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.) · capital Uxellodunum</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Gallic people of Quercy whose hill fort of Uxellodunum was the last stronghold to resist Caesar, in 51 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Cadurci lived in the valley of the Lot and its limestone plateaus, in the modern Lot. They were clients of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/arverni">Arverni</a> and produced linen famous in the Roman world.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Their leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucterius">Lucterius</a> was one of the most active commanders of the revolt of 52 BCE, raising peoples of the south to threaten the Roman Province.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 51 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucterius">Lucterius</a> and the Senonian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drappes">Drappes</a> held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-uxellodunum">Uxellodunum</a>, probably the Puy d'Issolud. Caesar cut off its water supply by tunnelling to the spring, and after the surrender he cut off the hands of the defenders as a warning. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> their town <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cahors">Divona</a> became Cahors.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/cadurci.jpg" alt="Cadurci" width="320" height="325"><figcaption>Image: User:Feitscherg · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Gallia_Tribes_Towns.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Uxellodunum</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Lucterius</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>France</dd></dl></aside></div>

